{
  "summary": "This study investigates nonreciprocal bending in ferroelectric membranes using suspended-membrane nanoindentation. It demonstrates asymmetric bending with a 33% difference in effective elastic modulus between opposite directions and polarity-dependent elastic recovery. The findings attribute this behavior to asymmetric ferroelectric domain switching driven by flexoelectricity, highlighting a novel nonreciprocal mechanism in ferroelectrics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Asymmetric bending in ferroelectric PbTiO3 membranes with a 3:1 elastic modulus difference between opposite directions",
    "Polarity-dependent elastic recovery after bending",
    "Nonreciprocal behavior originates from asymmetric ferroelectric domain switching via flexoelectricity"
  ],
  "study_type": "Suspended-membrane nanoindentation",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies flexoelectricity as a key mechanism for inducing nonreciprocal mechanical responses in ferroelectrics, expanding the understanding of unconventional mechanical behaviors in these materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a brain-targeted PEGylated ginsenoside Rg1 derivative (Rg1s-PEG-600) for Alzheimer's disease treatment. Using covalent conjugation to enhance blood-brain barrier permeability, the derivative reduced reactive oxygen species, inhibited NLRP1/3 inflammasome-mediated pyroptosis, and improved cognitive deficits in both acute neuroinflammation models and chronic 5xFAD mice. The findings demonstrate its efficacy in disrupting ROS-driven inflammatory cascades and neurodegeneration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Rg1s-PEG-600 enhanced brain accumulation and reduced ROS in neuroinflammation models",
    "Inhibition of NLRP1/3 inflammasome-mediated pyroptosis in the brain",
    "Reversal of spatial memory decline and synaptic loss in 5xFAD mice"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo models",
  "scientific_significance": "This nanotherapeutic strategy provides a multitarget approach to disrupt oxidative stress and neuroinflammatory pathways in Alzheimer's disease, offering a potential solution for BBB-impermeable therapeutics."
}

{
  "summary": "The study investigates how cellular self-organization regulates ferroptosis propagation. Using in silico and pharmacological approaches, it demonstrates that spatial patterns of cell density and alignment encode transcriptional programs, creating ferro: sensitive regions (low-density, misaligned) and propagation-resistant boundaries (high-density, aligned). These patterns constrain ferroptosis spread through polarized lipid distribution and YAP/TEAD1 or NRF2 activity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Low-density, misaligned regions with elevated YAP/TEAD1 activity are ferroptosis-sensitive",
    "High-density, aligned regions with increased NRF2 expression form propagation-resistant boundaries",
    "Polarized lipid distribution at cell poles creates peroxidation hotspots driving anisotropic ferroptosis propagation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In silico and pharmacological perturbations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cellular self-organization as a systems-level mechanism that constrains ferroptosis propagation, offering a framework for understanding tissue-scale regulation of cell death in development and disease."
}

{
  "summary": "The study investigates uniform lithium deposition on polycrystalline copper current collectors by engineering dislocation defects and crystal textures. It demonstrates that high-density geometrically necessary dislocations and enriched <110>/<111> textures enable thermodynamically favorable lithium nucleation and surface diffusion, leading to stable deposition and over 1200 cycles with high Coulombic efficiency. This approach addresses a critical challenge in lithium metal batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Densely distributed dislocations provide thermodynamically favorable lithium adsorption sites and heterogeneous nucleation sites",
    "Enriched <110>/<111> textures promote lithium surface diffusion and lateral growth",
    "Optimized Cu foils sustain over 1200 cycles with 99.52% average Coulombic efficiency in Li||Cu cells"
  ],
  "study_type": "Experimental with theoretical calculations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes dislocation-mediated nucleation as a fundamental design principle for achieving stable lithium deposition on practical copper current collectors, advancing the understanding of interfacial mechanisms in lithium metal batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines how biomaterials can target cell-free DNA (cfDNA) to mitigate inflammation by scavenging it. It evaluates the progression from free nucleases to advanced nanostructured platforms that sequester, degrade, or modulate cfDNA. The study highlights that while preclinical evidence supports efficacy, clinical translation requires standardized measurement, biofluid testing, and prospective trials to ensure selective cf:DNA removal without impairing host immunity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Biomaterials have evolved from simple nucleases to nanostructured platforms for targeted cfDNA scavenging",
    "Material architecture influences cfDNA accessibility, stability, tissue distribution, and therapeutic efficacy",
    "Preclinical evidence for cfDNA scavenging efficacy exists but clinical translation requires standardized measurement and prospective trials"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances the understanding of cfDNA as a therapeutic target in inflammation by demonstrating how biomaterial design can selectively remove pathogenic cfDNA while maintaining host immune function, providing a foundation for clinical translation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the functional impact of RNA editing in coleoid cephalopods by analyzing the Doryteuthis pealeii proteome. Using integrated proteomics and biochemical assays, it confirmed 7,997 recoded sites and demonstrated how RNA editing alters protein stability, localization, post-translational modifications, and enzymatic activity. Recoding of the E3 ligase MARCHF5 was shown to disrupt mitochondrial homeostasis, highlighting RNA editing's role in cellular physiology.",
  "key_findings": [
    "7,99:997 recoded sites confirmed at the protein level in coleoid cephalopods",
    "RNA editing alters protein stability, subcellular localization, and post-translational modifications",
    "Recoding of the E3 ligase MARCHF5 perturbs mitochondrial homeostasis"
  ],
  "study_type": "Proteome-scale analysis with integrated biochemical assays",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a comprehensive framework for understanding how RNA editing diversifies protein function and influences cellular physiology through proteome-wide recoding events."
}

{
  "summary": "This review explores Anatomically Accessible Local mRNA Therapeutics (ALmT), distinguishing them from systemic delivery methods. It examines site-specific barriers and engineering strategies for localized diseases, emphasizing protein restoration, supplementation, and tissue repair. The framework aims to enable targeted mRNA therapies without systemic circulation, improving efficacy for tissue-confined conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ALmT targets localized diseases with tissue-specific delivery methods like topical or intra-articular administration",
    "The framework enables protein restoration and tissue repair without systemic circulation",
    "ALmT applications include cytokine supplementation and regenerative modulation for localized pathologies"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes a conceptual framework for designing mRNA therapies that operate locally within tissues, potentially enhancing efficacy for diseases confined to specific anatomical sites without systemic immune activation."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines the evolution and design principles of cardiovascular occluders for interventional therapy, covering congenital heart defects and left atrial appendage closure. It compares non-degradable metals (e.g., stainless steel) to nitinol alloys and biodegradable polymers (e.g., polylactic acid), highlighting surface modifications for endothelialization and challenges in degradation kinetics. The study identifies key advancements in materials and design that enhance safety and efficacy for structural heart disease treatment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nitinol alloys offer hyperelasticity for self-expanding devices in transcatheter closure procedures.",
    "Surface nanocoatings of bioceramics like titanium nitride promote rapid endothelialization on nitinol implants.",
    "Biodegradable polymers such as polylactic acid and polydioxanone enable device design strategies to overcome hyperelasticity limitations."
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides a comprehensive synthesis of material innovations and design principles that advance the safety and efficacy of interventional therapies for structural heart disease, addressing critical challenges in device performance and biocompatibility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a photoswitchable opioid agonist, azo-morphine-3 (AM- 3), that reversibly switches between low and high efficacy states via light to optically control mu-opioid receptor signaling. The compound demonstrated reversible pain relief in mice with reduced side effects due to limited brain accumulation and localized activation, offering a potential strategy for targeted analgesia without systemic toxicity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AM-3 reversibly switches between low and high efficacy states of mu-opioid receptor signaling using light",
    "The compound provides reversible pain relief in multiple mouse pain models",
    "AM-3 exhibits reduced side effects due to minimal brain accumulation and localized activation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo mouse model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a photoswitchable opioid agonist platform for precise, reversible control of analgesia with reduced systemic side effects, advancing optogenetic approaches to targeted pain management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a strategy for synchronizing ablation of multifocal orthotopic breast tumors using multi-channel lanthanide nanocomposites. The approach leverages orthogonally controlled drug release (pH-responsive mitoxantrone and glutathathione-responsive paclitaxel) with real-time monitoring via upconversion luminescence. Small animal experiments demonstrated effective tumor ablation with minimal overtherapy risk.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Multi-channel lanthan:ide nanocomposites enable orthogonally controlled drug release for multifocal tumors",
    "Real-time monitoring of pH-responsive mitoxantrone release and glutathione-responsive paclitaxel release via upconversion luminescence",
    "Synchronized ablation of multiple orthotopic breast tumors with high efficiency and low overtherapy risk in small animal models"
  ],
  "study_type": "Small animal experiments",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a customizable therapeutic strategy for multifocal tumors through integrated drug release and real-time monitoring, advancing precision oncology approaches for heterogeneous tumor populations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated 3D-bioprinted nerve conduits incorporating NGF and VEGF to enhance peripheral nerve repair. Using a rat sciatic nerve defect model, the researchers designed a multichannel conduit with alginate, GelMA, BNC, and NGF/VEGF-loaded PLGA nanospheres. The conduit promoted neurovascular co-regeneration by activating PI3K/AKT and MAPK/ER. Results showed improved microvessel density, myelin integrity, and functional recovery compared to controls, with outcomes approaching autograft standards.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Increased microvessel density and S100β/NF200 signals in the NGF+VEGF+SC-SHED group",
    "Improved myelin morphometry and electrophysiological outcomes",
    "Enhanced gastrocnemius muscle preservation and functional recovery"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo rat sciatic nerve defect model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that integrated neurovascular guidance via 3D-bioprinted conduits with dual growth factors can effectively support coordinated nerve regeneration, providing a promising strategy for complex peripheral nerve repair."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated molecular responses to chronic exercise using multi-omics profiling in mice. Researchers analyzed 22 tissues and plasma from mice undergoing 8 weeks of voluntary wheel running, comparing active and inactive phases. Key findings include exercise-induced fiber-type switching in skeletal muscle, tissue-specific remodeling with greater changes during active phases, and sex-biased epigenetic responses. The study resolved cell-type-specific mechanisms underlying exercise adaptations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Exercise induced canonical fiber-type switching and widespread tissue-specific remodeling, with skeletal muscle showing the largest transcriptomic changes",
    "Most tissues exhibited greater molecular changes during active exercise phases, except hypothalamus, kidney, and lung",
    "Cell-type-resolved epigenetic analysis revealed sex-biased demethylation patterns linked to fiber-type switching in skeletal muscle"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse model with 8 weeks of voluntary wheel running",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a comprehensive multi-omics atlas of exercise-induced molecular adaptations across organs, revealing cell-type-specific mechanisms that were previously undetectable by bulk analyses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates radiative cooling floating covers to suppress lake evaporation. By designing Superhydrophobic Radiative Cooling Covers (SRCC) with high solar reflectance, strong mid-infrared emission, and superhydrophobicity, the researchers achieved 93.1% evaporation suppression at 91% coverage, exceeding conventional cover efficiency (ηeff/Φ > 1.0). SRCC reduced water temperature by 2.2°C and could increase freshwater reserves by 10.78 km³ across China annually.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SRCC achieves 93.1% evaporation suppression at 91% coverage with 2.2°C water temperature reduction",
    "SRCC yields ηeff/Φ > 1.0, surpassing conventional cover efficiency limits",
    "Large-scale simulations indicate 10.78 km³ annual freshwater reserve increase across China"
  ],
  "study_type": "Experimental and simulation",
  "scientific_significance": "SRCC provides the first engineering solution to exceed conventional evaporation suppression limits through radiative cooling, offering a scalable method to mitigate thermal accumulation in lakes and enhance freshwater storage under climate change."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cryogenic sintering of decellularized extracellular matrix (ECM) particles to create porous 3D scaffolds for large traumatic injuries. By controlling particle concentration and freezing rate, the method achieved tunable porosity (934-3476 μm² pore area) and mechanical stability. In vivo, scaffolds bridged tissue deficits with rapid macrophage infiltration and sustained interleukin-4 expression, particularly in optimized conditions, promoting Type 2 immune responses and tissue remodeling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cryogenic sintering of ECM particles enabled tunable 3D porosity (934-3476 μm² pore area) without altering biochemical composition.",
    "Optimized scaffolds (100 mg/mL, -80 °C) showed rapid CD206+ macrophage infiltration (4752 ± 1773 macrophages/mm²) and prolonged interleukin-4 expression (up to 8 weeks).",
    "Small-pored scaffolds degraded faster and remodeled into adipose tissue within 8-18 weeks post-implantation."
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that ECM particulates can be engineered into mechanically robust, porosity-tunable scaffolds that sustain Type 2 immune responses and tissue remodeling, advancing biomaterial design for large soft tissue defects."
}

{
  "summary": "This study designed mitochondria-targeted tetraoxane compounds (WMK-1/2) to induce ferroptosis by initiating lipid peroxidation without targeting GPX4 or FSP1. The compounds localized to mitochondria, caused local lipid peroxidation, impaired oxidative phosphorylation, and triggered a 'mito-ferroptosis' pathway that requires labile Fe2+ and is suppressed by α-lipoic acid. WMK-1/2 showed tumor suppression efficacy in cancer models and enhanced immune-checkpoint blockade.",
  "key_findings": [
    "WMK-1/2 are mitochondria-targeted tetraoxanes that initiate lipid peroxidation to drive ferroptosis",
    "The 'mito-ferroptosis' pathway skips GPX4 inhibition and requires labile Fe2+ for cell death",
    "WMK-1/2 suppress tumor growth and augment immune-checkpoint blockade efficacy in cancer models"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo cancer models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a protein-targeting-independent metabolic strategy for ferroptosis induction, offering a novel approach to overcome limitations in current ferroptosis-targeted cancer therapies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing photocatalytic acetylene semi-hydrogenation efficiency by optimizing interfacial electron transfer. Using benzotriazole-coordinated Ni single atoms in C3N4, the researchers demonstrated rapid electron transfer via upshifted Ni d-band centers and strengthened orbital overlap with adsorbed acetylene. The catalyst achieved high ethylene selectivity (97.6%) and production rate (32.29 mmol gcat⁻¹ h⁻¹) under solar light, outperforming conventional Ni SAs-C3N4 by ∼4×.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BTA-coordinated Ni single atoms in C3N4 facilitate rapid interfacial electron transfer for acetylene semi-hydrogenation",
    "Upshifting of Ni d-band center and enhanced orbital overlap with adsorbed C2H2 improve electron transfer kinetics",
    "BTA-Ni SAs-C3N4 achieves 97.6% ethylene selectivity and 32.29 mmol gcat⁻¹ h⁻¹ production rate under solar irradiation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In situ spectroscopic and theoretical analysis of photocatalytic systems",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanism for optimizing interfacial charge transfer in photocatalytic acetylene hydrogenation, providing a general strategy for designing efficient catalysts through precise atomic-level coordination."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a nanostructured gradient Ta-O-F coating on 316L stainless steel to address early bacterial infection and poor osseointegration in orthopedic implants. The coating features a corrosion-stable Ta2O5 barrier layer and an underlying fluoride reservoir to regulate ion release. Results showed improved corrosion resistance, moderated fluoride release, enhanced antibacterial activity against common pathogens, and promoted osteoblastic and endothelial responses in vitro and in infected rat models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Moderated fluoride release from the gradient coating suppressed burst exposure while maintaining antibacterial efficacy against S. aureus and E. coli",
    "The coating enhanced osteoblastic adhesion, proliferation, matrix mineralization, and vascularization in vitro",
    "In infected rat models, the coating reduced bacterial burden and inflammation while improving bone architecture compared to unmodified 316L SS"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a barrier-reservoir strategy for synchronizing anti-infective and osteoregenerative responses on metallic implants, addressing a critical challenge in orthopedic implant failure."
}

{
  "summary": "This study conducted a phenome-wide association study (PheWAS) across 13,322 traits using structural variants (SVs) from 467,1.52 UK Biobank genomes to assess their phenotypic impact. It identified 28,184 SV-trait associations, with 82.25% of SVs previously undetected by copy-number variant studies. The findings highlight SVs' significant but undercharacterized role in human health and disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "82.25% of SVs were outside the detectable range of prior copy-number variant studies",
    "28,184 associations between SVs and human health traits were detected",
    "32.21% of SVs at known genome-wide association study loci overlapped functional genomic regions"
  ],
  "study_type": "Phenome-wide association study (PheWAS)",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates the extensive phenotypic impact of structural variants, revealing their underestimated contribution to human health and disease and providing a resource for understanding genetic mechanisms underlying complex traits."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates voltage hysteresis in oxygen-redox cathodes, identifying quasi-flat bands as the origin of hysteresis exceeding 1 V during initial cycles. By linking weak lattice distortions and thermal vibrations to amplified band dispersion, the research proposes stabilizing symmetry and engineering orbital hybridization to mitigate hysteresis, enhancing energy efficiency for high-energy lithium batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Oxygen 2p states near the Fermi level in quasi-flat bands are sensitive to minor lattice distortions",
    "Weak perturbations disproportionately amplify band dispersion, causing voltage hysteresis",
    "Stabilizing symmetry and engineering orbital hybridization reduce hysteresis for practical battery operation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Theoretical modeling and design principles",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a fundamental mechanism for voltage hysteresis in oxygen-redox cathodes, providing a design framework to enhance energy efficiency in high-capacity lithium batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated enhancing NB-UVB phototherapy for psoriasis by integrating microneedles with high UV transmittance and calcipotriol delivery. The approach combined UVMNs to improve UV penetration and reduce dosage, with calcip. The mouse model showed improved symptoms through reduced keratinocyte proliferation and immune modulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Microneedles with high UV transmittance increased NB-UVB penetration into psoriatic skin",
    "Calcipotriol release suppressed keratinocyte proliferation within minutes",
    "Integrated therapy reduced NB-UVB dosage while improving symptom amelioration in mice"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse model",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach demonstrates a dual-modality strategy to overcome limitations of conventional NB-UVB therapy by enhancing delivery efficiency and reducing photodamage risk without compromising efficacy."
}

{
  "summary": "The study investigates the mechanism behind sex-based differences in chronic liver disease (CLD) using metabolomics data from 9,254 individuals. It identifies isoursodeoxycholic acid (isoUDCA) as a mediator of female hepatoprotection, originating from a bacterial consortium enriched by estrogen. The bile acid promotes SREBP2 nuclear accumulation, enhancing cholesterol handling via STARD4 and CYP7B1. This microbiome-bile acid-liver axis may explain sex disparities in CL. The findings suggest isoUDCA as a potential therapeutic target.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IsoUDCA, an endogenous bile acid, mediates female hepatoprotection in chronic liver disease.",
    "Estrogen selectively enriches a bacterial consortium that produces isoUDCA.",
    "IsoUDCA promotes SREBP2 nuclear accumulation to enhance intracellular cholesterol handling."
  ],
  "study_type": "Metabolomics analysis of large-scale human data",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a microbiome-bile acid-liver axis that explains sex-based differences in chronic liver disease susceptibility, providing a mechanistic basis for potential sex-specific therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the synthesis of bulk superconducting LiNbO2 crystals via CaH2 reduction of LiNbO3. The approach involves reducing Nb valence from 5+ to 3+ to induce a structural transformation, resulting in a superconducting phase with Tc onset up to : 14.4 K. Magnetization measurements confirm bulk superconductivity with ≈77% superconducting volume fraction and an upper critical field near 26 T.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Synthesis of bulk superconducting LiNbO2 crystals via CaH2 reduction of LiNbO3",
    "Reduction of Nb valence from 5+ to 3+ induces structural transformation and superconductivity with Tc onset up to 14.4 K",
    "Bulk superconductivity confirmed with ≈77% superconducting volume fraction and upper critical field near 26 T"
  ],
  "study_type": "Bulk phase transformation via CaH2 reduction",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that extreme hydride reduction can induce non-topochemical phase transformations to achieve bulk superconductivity with high critical field and volume fraction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered ultrasound-activatable artificial dendritic cells (nDC-M) with semiconducting polymers, hypoxia-cleavable IL-2 release, and tumor-targeting capabilities to enhance cancer immunotherapy. The system ablates tumors via sonodynamic effects, releases IL-2 under ultrasound, and suppresses metastasis in breast and lung cancer models, achieving complete tumor eradication when combined with checkpoint blockade.",
  "key_findings": [
    "nDC-M integrates semiconducting polymer nanoparticles for sonodynamic tumor ablation and hypoxia-cleavable IL-2 release",
    "The system enables tumor-specific antigen capture and ultrasound-triggered cytokine secretion",
    "Combination with checkpoint blockade eradicates tumors and induces long-term immunological memory"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo models",
  "scientific_significance": "This modular nanosystem demonstrates spatiotemporally controlled multifunctionality in immunosuppressive tumor environments, advancing targeted cancer immunotherapy through ultrasound-responsive design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how extracellular L-carnitine from muscle injury or red meat ingestion triggers inflammation via the pyrin inflammasome. Using LPS-challenged mice and LPS-primed macrophages, researchers found that L-carnitine uptake through OCTN2 represses mevalonate synthesis, activating the pyrin inflammasome. The inflammatory response to muscle injury requires both pyrin and OCTN2, suggesting L-carnitine acts as a biomarker for skeletal myocyte damage.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Extracellular L-carnitine activates the pyrin inflammasome in LPS-challenged mice and macrophages",
    "OCTN2-mediated uptake of L-carnitine represses mevalonate synthesis, triggering pyrin inflammasome activation",
    "The inflammatory response to skeletal muscle injury depends on pyrin and OCTN2"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies using LPS-challenged mice and LPS-primed macrophages",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies L-carnitine as a biomarker for skeletal myocyte damage that links dietary red meat intake to inflammatory disease via pyrin inflammasome activation."
}
